## Workout View Specification

The main view where users track daily exercise completion.

### Layout Structure

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│         WEEK 2 / 8        [←] [→]   │  ← WeekNavigator (Card)
│                                     │
│  Weekly Progress              0%    │
│  [████░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░░]   │  ← WeeklyProgressCard
│  Sets: 0/43              Keep Going!│
└─────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─ Exercises ─┬─ Workouts ─┬─ Active ─┐ [⊞/≡]  ← Tabs + ViewToggle
└─────────────┴────────────┴──────────┘

┌─────────────────────────────────────┐
│  ExerciseCard (see above)           │  ← Repeating list
└─────────────────────────────────────┘

┌─ Completed Exercises (1) ──────── ∧ ┐  ← CompletedSection (collapsible)
└─────────────────────────────────────┘

│  Start Workout (2 Exercises)        │  ← SelectionBar (Phase 2, sticky)
└─────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### WeekNavigator

```tsx
<Card className="rounded-2xl border-0 shadow-sm bg-gradient-to-r from-card to-card/80">
  <CardContent className="flex items-center justify-between p-4">
    <Button 
      variant="ghost" 
      size="icon"
      className="h-10 w-10 rounded-full hover:bg-primary/10 active:scale-90 transition-all"
      disabled={currentWeek <= 1}
      onClick={() => { setWeek(w => w - 1); triggerHaptic('light'); }}
    >
      <ChevronLeft className="h-6 w-6" />
    </Button>
    
    <div className="text-center">
      <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Week</p>
      <p className="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">
        {currentWeek} <span className="text-muted-foreground font-normal">/ {totalWeeks}</span>
      </p>
    </div>
    
    <Button 
      variant="ghost" 
      size="icon"
      className="h-10 w-10 rounded-full hover:bg-primary/10 active:scale-90 transition-all"
      disabled={currentWeek >= totalWeeks}
      onClick={() => { setWeek(w => w + 1); triggerHaptic('light'); }}
    >
      <ChevronRight className="h-6 w-6" />
    </Button>
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

